<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: HORSE RACING-IRISH GRAND NATIONAL STEEPLECHASE RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-IRISH GRAND NATIONAL STEEPLECHASE RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the grade one Irish</p>
<p>Grand National steeplechase run over three miles and five</p>
<p>furlongs (5.8 km) at Fairyhouse on Monday:</p>
<p> 1. Mudahim	13-2 (ridden by Jason Titley)</p>
<p> 2. Amble Speedy 14-1 (Francis Woods)</p>
<p> 3. The Grey Monk 9-2 favourite (Tony Dobbin)</p>
<p> 4. Papillon	6-1 (Charlie Swann)</p>
<p>20 ran.</p>
<p>Distances: Short head, 11 lengths, 2 lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by the In Touch Racing Club and trained in</p>
<p>England by Jenny Pitman.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 62,700 Irish pounds ($98,320).</p>
</text>
